  Named mathematical values can index types. The topology and endpoints below
  are explicit parameters; no ambient topology is selected implicitly.

Result subset element reflexivity:
  Attribution: topology; subset element reflexivity; original
  Let X: Type
  Let S: Set(X)
  Let x: Element(X,S)
  Conclude: x = x

Result path reflexivity:
  Attribution: topology; path reflexivity; original
  Let X: Type
  Let t: Topology(X)
  Let x,y: X
  Let p be a path from x to y in X with topology t
  Conclude: p = p

Result constant path exists:
  Attribution: topology; constant path exists; original
  Let X: Type
  Let t: Topology(X)
  Conclude:
    for every (x: X,
      there exists (p: Path(X,t,x,x), p = p))

Result named subset expression:
  Attribution: topology; named subset expression; original
  Let X,Y: Type
  Let f: Function(X,Y)
  Let S: Set(Y)
  Let T = inverse image(f,S)
  Let x be an element of T in X
  Conclude: x = x

